<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.325 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.325 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE JAN 31, 2002</p>
<p>			     $12.503 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.325    Awarded At	99.683	6.250</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.307    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.273    73 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.42 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Jan.02</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Jan.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 23.Jan.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  12.503 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272G7</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   30.305			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   632.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.250</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  700.00 MLN		     PRICE	 99.683</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.273-6.325 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.325</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD UP FROM 6.165 PCT AT AUCTION ON 19.DEC.96</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD HIGHEST SINCE 6.409 PCT AT AUCTION 26.SEP.96</p>
